              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A $19.99 jar and a $31.99 tub hold very different amounts of protein. Divide the price by the total grams of protein in the container and multiply by 25. That cost per 25 g figure is the only fair way to compare Simple Truth with name brands.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming the house brand is tested</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Simple Truth carries claims such as gluten-free and non-GMO, but we found no NSF or Informed Sport certification for its powders. If you are drug-tested, buy a certified flavor of a name brand and check the registry on the day.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Driving over without checking stock</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Many Kroger protein listings showed items out of stock or pickup unavailable at the store selected. Check the Kroger app for your own store before you make a special trip for one tub.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring digital coupons</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Kroger's weekly digital coupons often take several dollars off a tub, which changes the ranking between Simple Truth and Gold Standard. Clip them in the app before checkout, because the shelf price alone will not apply them.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying the greens version by default</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Simple Truth Protein with Greens costs more per tub than the plain plant powder, and the listing does not state the greens dose. Unless you specifically want the greens, the plain tub is the better buy.
              </p>
            </div>
